WEBVTT

00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:16,820
We're looking at my blood test and tumor markers, which one is most important?

00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:23,300
So a lot of people will get tumor markers done.

00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:29,100
If you got them done through us, I have put together the female tumor marker panel and

00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:30,580
the male tumor marker panel.

00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:33,220
Now, again, what are tumor markers?

00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:37,900
There are proteins that cancers can give off.

00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:43,940
Now, the operative word there is can, or may give off, maybe that's better grammar.

00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:50,180
They may, certain cancers may expel these different proteins, and then we can measure

00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:51,180
them.

00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:52,180
But they don't always.

00:00:52,180 --> 00:01:01,100
You could have stage 4 raging cancer and not show any positive lab test elevations of

00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:02,100
tumor markers.

00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:03,100
Why?

00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:04,100
But I don't know.

00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:06,100
It's just what it is.

00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:13,980
But it can be used if you do show elevations in tumor markers with your cancer.

00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:22,540
It can be used as another objective scale that you can measure progress in any course of care.

00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:25,100
So which ones are most important?

00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:30,020
Well, it partly depends on what type of cancer you have.

00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:36,620
So the female tumor marker panel is, I remember off the top of my head, it's CA-153.

00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:40,740
Now, CA-153 is only going to really show up in breast cancer.

00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:41,740
CA-199.

00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:49,220
CA-199 can show up in breast cancer, but it's a primary marker of pancreatic cancer.

00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:58,320
CA-25-27, or 27-29, that's only going to be, well, it's usually going to be just breast

00:01:58,320 --> 00:01:59,320
cancer.

00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:05,920
CA-153 is, can be across multiple different cancers.

00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:11,200
And CA-125, which could also be positive in multiple different cancers.

00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:12,800
Which one is most important?

00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:15,240
There is one that's most important.

00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:23,080
So whichever shows up on you, and we want to use that as a marker, well, what if this shows

00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:24,080
up and this doesn't?

00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:26,680
This one went up and this one went down.

00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:30,880
Again, you're just using those as clues to what's going on.

00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:35,000
Remember, any blood test, any test is just a clue.

00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,040
It's just giving us clues of what could be going on.

00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:45,140
You're helping that with looking at other objective and subjective data to come up with the differential

00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:52,480
diagnosis of which direction you think the cancer is going and what interventions might be

00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,480
the wisest to take.

00:02:54,480 --> 00:03:00,080
So there isn't the cancer marker or tumor marker that's more important than the other.

00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:02,680
We're just looking at changes in that.

